From 4726e7a73aa30d083e0735bcbe7d2a5d1f92d61a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DByte308 <69403407+DByte308@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 07:42:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 21/28] d/pimax_p3c, st/oxr: FOV levels and sized foveation
 quad views

PIMAX_FOV_PERCENT (50-100) narrows the view tangents and the recommended
render size by the same ratio (selectable FOV levels). The emulated quad
view config no longer copies the full stereo size into the inset: the inset
gets the stereo pixel density over its angles (from one get_view_poses(QUAD)
call, so the driver is the single source of truth for the inset FOV) times
XRT_FOVEATION_INSET_DENSITY_PERCENT; context views are scaled by
XRT_FOVEATION_CONTEXT_PERCENT. XRT_FOVEATION_INSET_DEG sets the inset size.

Behaviour change: quad-view apps now get a much smaller inset image at 100 %
density instead of a second full-resolution copy of each eye.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
